      "text": "1304087.</answer>.<|User|>The answer is correct. Now, please solve another problem.\nQuestion: What is the product of 972672 and 331315? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 972672 and 331315, we can follow these steps:.\n1. Use the standard algorithm for multiplication, which involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results.\n2. Start by multiplying the numbers as if they were single digits, then gradually increase the size of the numbers being multiplied.\n3. Keep track of the place values and add the appropriate number of zeros at the end of the final product.\nLet's perform the multiplication:.\n```.\n  972672.\n\u00d7  331315.\n---------.\n```.\nStarting with the rightmost column:.\n2 \u00d7 5 = 10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n2 \u00d7 1 + 1 (carry) = 3.\n2 \u00d7 3 + 1 (carry) = 7.\n2 \u00d7 1 + 1 (carry) = 3.\n2 \u00d7 3 + 1 (carry) = 7.\n2 \u00d7 9 = 18, write down 8 and carry over 1.\nNext column:.\n7 \u00d7 5 = 35, write down 5 and carry over 3.\n7 \u00d7 1 + 3 (carry) = 10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n7 \u00d7 3 + 1 (carry) = 22, write down 2 and carry over 2.\n7 \u00d7 1 + 2 (carry) = 9.\n7 \u00d7 3 + 2 (carry) = 23, write down 3 and carry over 2.\n7 \u00d7 9 = 63, write down 3 and carry over 6.\nNext column:.\n6 \u00d7 5 = 30, write down 0 and carry over 3.\n6 \u00d7 1 + 3 (carry) = 9.\n6 \u00d7 3 + 3 (carry) = 21, write down 1 and carry over 2.\n6 \u00d7 1 + 2 (carry) = 8.\n6 \u00d7 3 + 2 (carry) = 22, write down 2 and carry over 2.\n6 \u00d7 9 = 54, write down 4 and carry over 5.\nNext column:.\n2 \u00d7 5 = 10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n2 \u00d7 1 + 1 (carry) = 3.\n2 \u00d7 3 + 1 (carry) = 7.\n2 \u00d7 1 + 1 (carry) = 3.\n2 \u00d7 3 + 1 (carry) = 7.\n2 \u00d7 9 = 18, write down 8 and carry over 1.\nNext column:.\n9 \u00d7 5 = 45, write down 5 and carry over 4.\n9 \u00d7 1 + 4 (carry) = 13, write